      "description": "Museum opened in 1935 to preserve the treasures of the Owari Tokugawa clan in Nagoya. Its collection includes the National Treasure Tale of Genji handscrolls, swords, armor and Noh masks, displayed beside the adjoining Tokugawa Garden.",
